{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And YHWH regretted that He had made.</b> There was regret before Him that He had created him among the lower beings — for had he been from the upper beings, he would have rebelled (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>And it grieved Him.</b> Man — to the heart of the Omnipresent: it rose in the thought of the Omnipresent to grieve him. This is the Targum of Onkelos. Another matter: וַיִּנָּחֶם — the thought of the Omnipresent turned from the attribute of mercy to the attribute of judgment; it rose in thought before Him what to do to man whom He had made on the earth. And so every expression of נִיחוּם in Scripture is an expression of reconsidering what to do: וּבֶן אָדָם וְיִתְנֶחָם (Numbers 23); וְעַל עֲבָדָיו יִתְנֶחָם (Deuteronomy 32); וַיִּנָּחֶם YHWH עַל הָרָעָה (Exodus 32); נִחַמְתִּי כִּי הִמְלַכְתִּי (1 Samuel 15) — all of them are an expression of changing thought." "<b>And it grieved Him to His heart.</b> He mourned over the destruction of the work of His hands, as in נֶעֱצַב הַמֶּלֶךְ עַל בְּנוֹ (ibid. 2:19). And this I wrote for the reply to the heretics — a certain nation that asked Rabbi Yehoshua ben Korcha. He said to him: Do you not acknowledge that the Holy One, blessed be He, foresees what is born? He said to him: Yes. He said to him: But is it not written וַיִּתְעַצֵּב אֶל לִבּוֹ? He said to him: A son was born to you in your days? He said to him: Yes. He said to him: And what did you do? He said to him: I rejoiced and made everyone rejoice. He said to him: But did you not know that his end is to die? He said to him: At the time of joy — joy; at the time of mourning — mourning. He said to him: Such is the way of the Holy One, blessed be He — even though it is revealed before Him that their end is to sin and to destruction, He did not refrain from creating them for the sake of the righteous destined to arise from them."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:45.829083729Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}